WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:20.129
Mrs. Rachel Lynde lived on the main road in Avonlea, a town on Prince Edward Island, off the coast of Canada.

2
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:26.764
Anybody who was coming to or leaving Avonlea had to use the main road and pass by the Lyndes' house.

3
00:00:26.765 --> 00:00:30.676
Mrs. Lynde was always watching from her kitchen window.

4
00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:34.683
Mrs. Lynde sat at her window one afternoon in early June.

5
00:00:34.684 --> 00:00:41.718
At half-past three, Matthew Cuthbert was driving his buggy down the road. He wore his best suit.

6
00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:47.412
"Matthew should be planting turnip seeds now like Mr. Lynde," thought Mrs. Lynde.

7
00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:51.825
"But instead he is in his buggy and dressed in his best suit!

8
00:00:51.826 --> 00:00:55.708
Where is Matthew Cuthbert going and why?"

9
00:00:55.709 --> 00:01:01.685
If it was any other man in Avonlea, Mrs. Lynde might be able to guess where he was going.

10
00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:06.869
But Matthew Cuthbert so rarely left home that it had to be something unusual.

11
00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:12.263
He was the shyest man alive and hated to go anywhere he might have to talk.

12
00:01:12.264 --> 00:01:19.444
"I'll just go to Green Gables and ask his sister, Marilla, where he's gone," she decided.

13
00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:25.521
After hearing "Come in!" from Marilla, Mrs. Lynde stepped into the kitchen.

14
00:01:25.522 --> 00:01:28.639
She looked carefully at everything on the table.

15
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.516
There were three plates, so Marilla must have been expecting a visitor to come home with Matthew.

16
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:42.949
But the dishes were everyday dishes and the cake was plain, so the expected visitor could not be anybody too important.

17
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.476
"Good evening, Rachel," Marilla greeted Mrs. Lynde.

18
00:01:46.477 --> 00:01:51.317
"This is a lovely evening, isn't it? Won't you sit down? How are you?"

19
00:01:51.318 --> 00:01:57.080
Marilla was tall and thin. Even though she looked stern, she did have a sense of humor.

20
00:01:57.081 --> 00:02:05.035
"We're well," said Mrs. Lynde. "Though I thought you weren't well when I saw Matthew in the buggy today."

21
00:02:05.036 --> 00:02:10.790
Marilla had expected Mrs. Lynde to visit because Mrs. Lynde was a curious person.

22
00:02:10.791 --> 00:02:14.136
"Matthew went to Bright River," Marilla said.

23
00:02:14.137 --> 00:02:18.935
"We're getting a little boy from an orphanage, and he's coming on the train tonight."

24
00:02:18.936 --> 00:02:26.569
If Marilla had said that Matthew had gone to meet a kangaroo from Australia, Mrs. Lynde could not be more surprised.

25
00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.945
She actually stopped talking for five seconds.

26
00:02:29.946 --> 00:02:34.736
"Why on earth would you do that?" she asked disapprovingly.

27
00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:40.196
"We've been thinking about it for some time—all winter, in fact," replied Marilla.

28
00:02:40.197 --> 00:02:45.524
"Matthew is growing older. He's sixty, and his heart is not so good.

29
00:02:45.525 --> 00:02:48.597
It's difficult to hire someone to do farm work."

30
00:02:48.598 --> 00:02:51.753
Mrs. Lynde always said what she thought.

31
00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:57.847
In this case it was, "Well, Marilla, I think you're doing a very foolish thing.

32
00:02:57.848 --> 00:03:02.399
You're bringing a strange child into your house and you don't know a thing about him!

33
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.326
Last week in the newspaper,

34
00:03:04.327 --> 00:03:13.478
it said that a family took an orphan boy and he set fire to the house at night—on purpose, Marilla—and nearly burnt them in their beds."

35
00:03:13.479 --> 00:03:16.550
Marilla was neither offended nor alarmed.

36
00:03:16.551 --> 00:03:22.153
Meanwhile Matthew Cuthbert and the horse jogged the ten kilometers to the station.

37
00:03:22.154 --> 00:03:27.951
It was a pretty road, and the air was sweet with the smell of apple and plum blossoms.

38
00:03:27.952 --> 00:03:32.303
When Matthew arrived, there was no train, and he thought he was early.

39
00:03:32.304 --> 00:03:37.557
The long platform was almost deserted, except for a girl sitting at the end.

40
00:03:37.558 --> 00:03:40.859
Matthew walked quickly past her to the station office.

41
00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:47.281
"The five-thirty train has gone, but there was a passenger for you, a little girl," said the stationmaster.

42
00:03:47.282 --> 00:03:52.639
"I'm not expecting a girl," said Matthew, surprised. "It's a boy I've come for."

43
00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.653
The stationmaster raised his eyebrows. "Well, I guess there's some mistake.

44
00:03:57.654 --> 00:04:00.301
Mrs. Spencer came off the train with that girl.

45
00:04:00.302 --> 00:04:04.426
She said you and your sister, Marilla, were adopting the girl from an orphanage."

46
00:04:04.427 --> 00:04:11.777
The girl watched Matthew. She was eleven years old and dressed in a very old and very ugly dress.

47
00:04:11.778 --> 00:04:14.781
On her head was a worn-out, brown hat.

48
00:04:14.782 --> 00:04:19.794
Under the hat were two braids of very thick, very red hair.

49
00:04:19.795 --> 00:04:24.758
Her face was small, white, and thin, and she had many freckles.

50
00:04:24.759 --> 00:04:32.412
"I suppose you are Mr. Matthew Cuthbert of Green Gables?" she said in a clear, sweet voice.

51
00:04:32.413 --> 00:04:36.441
She held out her hand. "I'm very glad to see you.

52
00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.775
I was afraid you weren't coming for me.

53
00:04:38.776 --> 00:04:44.496
I had decided if you didn't come for me, I'd climb up that big wild cherry tree.

54
00:04:44.497 --> 00:04:49.976
It would be lovely to sleep in a wild cherry tree under the moon, don't you think?"

55
00:04:49.977 --> 00:04:54.506
Matthew shook the little hand awkwardly and wondered what to say.

56
00:04:54.507 --> 00:05:00.588
Matthew could not say there was a mistake; he would take her home and let Marilla explain everything.

57
00:05:00.589 --> 00:05:03.495
"I'm sorry I was late," he said shyly.

58
00:05:03.496 --> 00:05:06.317
"Come along. The horse is over in the yard."

59
00:05:06.318 --> 00:05:12.719
"Oh, I'm very glad you came," the girl said, "even if it would be nice to sleep in a cherry tree.

60
00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.241
It's wonderful I'm going to live with you and belong to you.

61
00:05:16.242 --> 00:05:19.533
I've never belonged to anybody—not really."

62
00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:23.158
The girl kept talking as they drove down the main road.

63
00:05:23.159 --> 00:05:30.907
"Isn't it beautiful?" she said. "I've always heard that Prince Edward Island is the prettiest place in the world.

64
00:05:30.908 --> 00:05:35.345
I used to imagine living here, but I never expected I actually would.

65
00:05:35.346 --> 00:05:40.493
Am I talking too much?" she went on. "People always tell me I do.

66
00:05:40.494 --> 00:05:45.696
If you say so, I'll stop. I can stop, though it is difficult."

67
00:05:45.697 --> 00:05:53.493
Surprisingly, Matthew was enjoying himself. He'd never expected to enjoy the company of a young girl.

68
00:05:53.494 --> 00:05:58.303
He said shyly, "Oh, you can talk as much as you like. I don't mind."

69
00:05:58.304 --> 00:06:05.018
"I'm so glad. You and I will get along just fine. I feel nearly perfectly happy.

70
00:06:05.019 --> 00:06:12.100
I can't feel perfectly happy because—well, what color is this?" The girl held up one of her braids.

71
00:06:12.101 --> 00:06:15.844
"It's red, isn't it?" he said.

72
00:06:15.845 --> 00:06:22.449
"Yes, it's red," she said, sighing. "Now you see why I can't be perfectly happy.

73
00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:25.625
Nobody with red hair can be perfectly happy."

74
00:06:25.626 --> 00:06:29.086
"We're near home now," Matthew said uneasily.

75
00:06:29.087 --> 00:06:35.230
As they approached Green Gables, he did not think about Marilla or himself or the mistake.

76
00:06:35.231 --> 00:06:47.839
He thought only about the child's disappointment when she discovered the truth.
